{
  "name": "rubble-debris-masonry",
  "label": "Rubble debris, masonry",
  "type": "graph",
  "parameters": {},
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "About",
      "type": "comment",
      "parameters": {},
      "node_position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -350
      },
      "size": {
        "x": 900,
        "y": 214
      },
      "title": "About this material",
      "text": "Rubble material: broken brick and masonry, about 6 m across, from a photographic study, built from sources/ (pigment and the 16-bit height fields). The rubble models' UVs set the ground one repeat covers. They tile seamlessly: keep them so. Relief is the heightmap's height range as a percentage of the repeat; the normals round it to a whole code of the heightmap (Relief x 25.5), so keep it a multiple of 10 / 255 (0.0392), and set the Material node's Depth scale to Relief / 25 (tools/materials/README.md). The ...PNG8 groups and the nodes after them only store exact file values; leave them. Export: File > Export material > Godot > Godot 4 Standard into data/models/board/textures/scenery, then Reload assets in the game's Tuning panel.",
      "color": {
        "type": "Color",
        "r": 0.14,
        "g": 0.24,
        "b": 0.3,
        "a": 1
      }
    },
